<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime exceptions for the Kernl .app.

  Notarization requires the hardened runtime (codesign, options runtime), and
  the hardened runtime kills exactly the things a JavaScript runtime does for a
  living. Each entry below is here because the payload needs it, not as a
  blanket loosening:

    allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory
        Bun and Node compile JavaScript to machine code at runtime and execute
        pages they wrote themselves. Without these the process is killed on the
        first hot function with EXC_BAD_ACCESS, which looks like a crash on
        launch rather than like a signing problem. Worth naming here for
        whoever debugs it at 2am.

    disable-library-validation
        The payload dlopen()s native addons (.node) and ships its own ffmpeg
        and whisper binaries. Library validation refuses any code not signed by
        the same Team ID: CI signs everything it ships, but a user extension
        bringing its own prebuilt addon would be refused at runtime.

    allow-dyld-environment-variables
        The launcher sets DYLD_* so the payload finds its bundled dylibs.

  If a future build drops the bundled binaries and the native addons, drop
  disable-library-validation with them. A smaller entitlement set is a smaller
  attack surface, and nothing here is free.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
